## PART 3 — Stock–bond diversification risk

The chapter identifies 1994 and 2022 as years when both US equities and Treasuries experienced negative nominal returns.

### Required data

Retrieve:

- S&P 500 total-return index.
- US Treasury total-return index.
- US CPI inflation.
- US 10-year breakeven inflation.
- US 10-year real Treasury yield.

### Candidate factor construction

**Factor 5 — Stock–bond rolling correlation**

Calculate the trailing 60-trading-day correlation between daily S&P 500 and US Treasury total returns.

`STOCK_BOND_CORR_60D(t) = Corr(R_SPX, R_UST)`

Use only observations available through time t.

**Factor 6 — Inflation-conditioned diversification regime**

Investigate whether the level or momentum of inflation compensation predicts subsequent stock–bond correlation.

Potential predictors:

- 10-year breakeven level.
- 60-day breakeven change.
- Real-yield momentum.
- CPI inflation trend, using publication-aware observations.

Evaluate whether these variables provide incremental information relative to the historical stock–bond correlation itself.

Do not assume that contemporaneous correlation predicts future correlation.

